        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "73aef42e-0833-51f7-901d-55c2c18bc442",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Bundeswettbewerb Gesang\n- Concepts: Operetta\n- People: Sebastian Noack, Dietrich Fischer-Dieskau, Aribert Reimann\n- Places: Berlin, Wigmore Hall\n- Events: International Song Competition\n\nFacts:\n- Beginning in 1979, the Bundeswettbewerb Gesang has been held annually.\n- In uneven years, the Bundeswettbewerb Gesang is held for the categories Musical and Chanson.\n- In even years, the Bundeswettbewerb Gesang is held for the categories Opera, Operetta, and concert singing.\n- Operetta is a genre of light opera, with “light” referring to both the music and the subject matter.\n- Before 1996, Sebastian Noack attended master classes with Dietrich Fischer-Dieskau and Aribert Reimann.\n- In 1996, Sebastian Noack won 1st prize at the Bundeswettbewerb Gesang in Berlin.\n- In 1997, Sebastian Noack was awarded 2nd prize at the International Song Competition at Wigmore Hall.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d4428635-a7d4-5fa1-be17-2d0f6a0917b4",
        "text": "Page: Bundeswettbewerb Gesang. Sentence: Beginning in 1979, it has been held annually, for the categories Musical and Chanson in uneven years, for Opera, Operetta and concert singing in even years.\nPage: Operetta. Sentence: Operetta is a genre of light opera, \"light\" in terms both of music and subject matter.\nPage: Sebastian Noack. Sentence: After attending master classes with Dietrich Fischer-Dieskau and Aribert Reimann, he won 1st prize at the Bundeswettbewerb Gesang in Berlin 1996 and was awarded 2nd prize at the International Song Competition at Wigmore Hall the following year.",
